'''Myykians'''<ref name="Neel's Species">{{WebCite|url=https://collider.com/star-wars-skeleton-crew-neel-species-myykian-explained|text=We Finally Officially Know What Species Neel Is in 'Star Wars: Skeleton Crew' [Exclusive&#93;|author=Blevins, Adam|date=2025-01-16|work=[[Wikipedia:Valnet#Collider|''Collider'']]|archivedate=20250116235915}}</ref> were a species of [[elephantine]] humanoids that lived in [[the galaxy]]. The [[species]] possessed [[Color|blue]] skin<ref name="Real Adventure" /> and was elephantine in appearance,<ref name="Elephantine" /> including a long trunk-like nose and two [[eye]]s. They could also possess a head of [[hair]]. The [[youngling]] [[Neel]] and [[Neel's family|his family]] were members of the species.<ref name="Real Adventure" />

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|And, no, Neel isn't the same species as Max Rebo. We asked.|[[Kristin Baver]], on [[StarWars.com]]|<ref name="Interview">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-jon-watts-christopher-ford-interview|text=With ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'', Jon Watts and Chris Ford are Ready for Their Own Pirate Adventure}}</ref>}}
The Myykian species<ref name="Neel's Species" /> was created for the character Neel, who appears in the live-action television series ''[[Star Wars: Skeleton Crew]]'', where he was portrayed by [[Robert Timothy Smith]] using a combination of facial motion capture on-set performance in a costume and an animatronic head.<ref name="Adventure Interview" /> In response to fan debate as to whether Neel was an [[Ortolan]] like [[Maximilian Rebo|Max Rebo]], [[Leland Chee]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] confirmed Neel's species was its own alien race,<ref name="Elephantine" /> which was later also confirmed by the series' creator [[Christopher Ford]].<ref name="Adventure Interview">{{SW|url=news/skeleton-crew-jon-watts-christopher-ford-interview|text=With ''Star Wars: Skeleton Crew'', Jon Watts and Chris Ford are Ready for Their Own Pirate Adventure}}</ref> The species was finally identified on [[January 16]], [[2025]], after [[The Real Good Guys|the season finale]], via a interview with [[Wikipedia:Valnet#Collider|''Collider'']],<ref name="Neel's Species" /> a name that was later also used by ''[[Star Wars Insider]]''.<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|234|Neel Nation: Robert Timothy Smith}}</ref>

